{"base_rate":0.3615819209039548,"brier":0.16647118644067796,"bss":0.2788473727876106,"bss_hi":0.4386123841236998,"bss_lo":0.06617386810828366,"chart":{"base":[374.6,169.2],"fp":[209.8,129.0],"lead":"62,240.3 272,223.3 482,210.1 692,196.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 48% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 38% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 1%; promised 99% → rained 73%"},"rel":"75.2,461.9 454.2,333.1 683.5,150"},"country":"NP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.1737099811676083,"ess":113.09592344068336,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kathmandu</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kathmandu rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>79%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 531 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-02-01. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 113 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(41&ndash;183) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>50</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>159</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kathmandu</b> <span class=\"muted\">Nepal</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;36% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 36% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>41&ndash;183\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>531 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kathmandu &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kathmandu\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.02269230769231,382.0 86.32,322.43636363636364 220.38111111111112,166.2962962962963 341.0584,54.39999999999998 394.23789473684207,18.0 411.91094339622646,18.0 411.91094339622646,20.289308176100633 394.23789473684207,56.31578947368422 341.0584,134.48 220.38111111111112,260.6666666666667 86.32,375.3818181818182 58.02269230769231,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"250.38418079096044\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"250.38418079096044\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.02269230769231,379.6666666666667 86.32,375.3818181818182 220.38111111111112,307.85185185185185 341.0584,229.12 394.23789473684207,177.64912280701756 411.91094339622646,93.54716981132071\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 156 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.02269230769231\" cy=\"379.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"86.32\" cy=\"375.3818181818182\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"220.38111111111112\" cy=\"307.85185185185185\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 50 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"341.0584\" cy=\"229.12\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"394.23789473684207\" cy=\"177.64912280701756\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 159 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.91094339622646\" cy=\"93.54716981132071\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(36%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":27.70169,"lon":85.3206,"n":531,"n_cities":216,"name":"Kathmandu","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":6.41025641025641e-05,"n":156,"obs":0.00641025641025641,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.07999999999999997,"n":55,"obs":0.01818181818181818,"sig":false},{"hi":0.69,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.4587037037037038,"n":54,"obs":0.2037037037037037,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.69,"mean":0.7996,"n":50,"obs":0.42,"sig":true},{"hi":0.980